From 33bf3003f1cc45b6aab0492131958716c54653e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:54:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEX: frame start pacing remembers 256 frames
 (VKD3D_FEX_START_WINDOW)

Outside GPU-bound pacing the hold-back now aims below the smallest
spare time of the last 256 frames (~8.5 s), not only the last 64
(~2 s). With fex14's 50 ms ceiling frames reached the screen 25-30 ms
sooner (start to screen ~42 ms calm, ~51 ms in play, was 70-76 ms), but
the hold-back made 83 frames late in 689 s (1 every ~8 s, was 1 every
~20 s). Standing still, the game's own frame took 15-30 ms instead of
~9 ms in 78 of 459 seconds, ~6 s apart on average; 2 s after one the
hold-back had grown back above the next. Replayed per frame on that
run, 256 frames make ~70% fewer frames late for ~4-5 ms less hold-back.
VKD3D_FEX_START_WINDOW takes 64-1024 (64 = fex14). The 64-frame ring
stays for GPU-bound pacing. The frame start line shows in how many
frames the longer memory held back less than the last 64 alone, and by
how much.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WZVGoVEaHJ78mpf2D3MiER
---
